se use: [l=Virgin]\r\nFor the UK branch please use: [l=Virgin Records Ltd.]\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:108701","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":750,"name":"Virgin"},"sublabels":[{"id":58020,"name":"Captive Records"},{"id":947703,"name":"Jackie (2)"},{"id":33703,"name":"Virgin Records America"}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/108701-Virgin-Records","type":"label","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/label/7801/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"7801","image":"https://i.discogs.com/mqNS-xVDEJc9jHhhxUjcB2e3LRRLok1w_bvSpz4RLuk/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:229/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTc4MDEt/MTQ4NDU1NzczMi0y/NDc0LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/FffY08nG-70VR6JMs3c_viWEuXZPFg_rS8I8bsiI6-4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTc4MDEt/MTQ4NDU1NzczMi0y/NDc0LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Ruthless Records was founded by rapper [a=Eazy-E] (supposedly with money he made as a drug dealer) and manager [a589451] (who died in 2016). It was the home of gangsta rap pioneers [a=N.W.A.], whose records were distributed through [l=Priority Records].\r\n\r\nThe majority of all Ruthless material was distributed by the [l=ATCO Records] division of [l=Atlantic Records] (particularly with acts such as [a=JJ Fad], [a=The D.O.C.] and [a=Michel'le]), while records by the group [a=Above The Law] and a fledgling young [a=Kokane] were released through [l=Epic].\r\nIn 1993, Ruthless dropped all ties with Priority, Atlantic and Epic and moved to [l=Relativity] for distribution, bringing with them a new era of artistry with the introduction of [a=Bone Thugs-N-Harmony].\r\n\r\nYears after Eazy-E's death from AIDS, the Ruthless label and back catalog (excluding the Michel'le and Bone-Thugs-N-Harmony material, which stayed with Atlantic and Sony Music respectively) was sold to longtime distributor Priority Records, which in turn was bought out by Capitol and became one of its subsidiaries.\r\n\r\nSince 2011, Ruthless Records was inactive for a short time, but was then relaunched in late 2015 by Eazy-E's widow, [a2503276].","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:7801","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":2715,"name":"Priority Records"},"sublabels":[{"id":67289,"name":"Comptown Records"}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/7801-Ruthless-Records","type":"label","urls":["https://www.ruthlessrecords.com/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruthless_Records"]}},"/api/discogs/release/10229775":{"cached":true,"release":{"artists":[{"id":null,"name":"Thelonious Monk"}],"formats":[],"genres":["Jazz"],"id":"10229775","images":[],"labels":[{"catno":"CK89175","id":1866,"name":"Columbia"}],"styles":["Hard Bop","Bop"],"title":"The Essential Thelonious Monk","tracklist":["'Round Midnight","Bemsha Swing","Blue Monk","Rhythm-A-Ning","Epistrophy","Crepuscule With Nellie","Misterioso","Brilliant Corners","Well You Needn't","Ruby, My Dear (Take 3)","Straight, No Chaser"],"uri":"https://www.discogs.com/release/10229775","videos":[],"year":2003}},"/api/discogs/release/10425953":{"cached":true,"release":{"artists":[{"id":null,"name":"Sports (9)"}],"formats":[],"genres":["Electronic"],"id":"10425953","images":[],"labels":[{"catno":"FIREC023","id":36714,"name":"Firecracker Recordings"}],"styles":["House","Breakbeat","Drum n Bass","Downtempo","Ambient"],"title":"Modern Species","tracklist":["World A","Stellar Clusters","Fertile Crescent","Entry Mode","Parallax","Ascension","For Real For You","Reluctant Memory"],"uri":"https://www.discogs.com/release/10425953","videos":[],"year":2017}},"/api/discogs/release/1061745/credits":{"cached":true,"credits":[{"id":841881,"name":"Jenny Owen Youngs","role":"Main Artist","type":"artist"},{"id":1263,"name":"Nettwerk","role":"Label","type":"label"},{"id":900714,"name":"Dan Romer","role":"Arranged By","type":"person"},{"id":1873378,"name":"Christie Little","role":"Design","type":"person"},{"id":2328525,"name":"Virginia Elwood","rol